    "f6951292f6422ee4": {
      "text": "CONTEXT: Signal defines an anchor-based KV-cache reuse contract: on edit V→V', re-prefill exactly [p, |V'|) where p = deepest anchor passing four checks (cumulative content hash, position-offset, model/template/tokenizer binding, KV-provenance); everything before p is bit-reused; deterministic validation; full recompute is the fallback. The brief's focus is edge cases, boundaries, invariants — so the deliverable must target the sharpest failure mode, not restate the happy path. ROLE: Inference-systems engineer designing the anchor-validation path for a KV-cache reuse engine. TASK: Specify the one mechanism that makes the four-check anchor selection correct at its hardest boundary, and the one test that can kill it. CONSTRAINTS: One mechanism, one sentence of significance, one falsifiable test. No architecture tours, no restating the contract, no unprompted extensions. Flag tri-state status of any empirical claim. Do not claim bit-identity is achieved — claim it is testable. INPUTS: The SIGNAL block only. No codebase, no benchmarks, no prior artifacts available in this session. SUCCESS: A reviewer building this engine can implement the validation path and the falsification harness directly from this output without asking a follow-up; the test would actually detect the named failure, not a proxy for it. OUTPUT: Task envelope + THE MECHANISM / WHY IT MATTERS / THE TEST. **THE MECHANISM — Provenance-stamped anchor ledger with deepest-first exact-match walk. Each anchor persists a 4-tuple: (a) xxh3-128 cumulative hash over the *actual token ids* of [0, p_anchor) — computed from V's tokens, not from a stored summary, so verification is exact re-hash over V'[0,p), not probabilistic; (b) physical offset p_anchor; (c) binding fingerprint (model revision + chat template hash + tokenizer hash + rope/position config); (d) provenance fingerprint (attention kernel identity + dtype + chunked-prefill chunk plan + any precision-affecting flag). On edit, walk anchors deepest-first; first entry where all four recomputed/stored keys match exactly wins; p = its offset; no match → p = 0 (full recompute, the safe fallback). Boundary cases handled explicitly: anchor at |V'| (edit truncated to an anchor) → empty prefill, reuse all; insertion strictly before every anchor → all cumulative hashes fail → p = 0; hash equality with offset mismatch (content moved) → rejected by check (b), never re-rotated. **WHY IT MATTERS:** The four checks are only sound if each one kills a distinct failure — hash kills content drift, offset kills position-shifted reuse (rotary positions would be wrong even for identical text), binding kills cross-model contamination, provenance kills bit-mismatch from numerically different prefill paths (chunked prefill is non-associative in float; same tokens, different chunk plan → different KV bits) — and dropping any one check silently converts a \"bit-reuse\" guarantee into approximate reuse wearing a correctness label. **THE TEST (falsifiable):** Build V with anchors at offsets 100 and 900 (same binding/provenance); apply an edit inserting 50 tokens at offset 500 — *between* the anchors. Falsification conditions, all machine-checkable: (1) engine must select p = 100, not 900 — a naive content-only matcher picks 900 (the anchor text still appears in V') and fails here; (2) KV for [0,100) must be byte-identical to a from-scratch prefill of V'[0:100); (3) full-sequence logits from the anchor path must be **bit-identical** to a full-recompute baseline of V' — a single ULP divergence kills the mechanism. Secondary kill-switch in the same harness: recompute the reference KV for [0,100) under a different chunk plan; if the engine reuses across that provenance mismatch instead of falling back to p = 0, the provenance check is decorative and the mechanism fails. **STATUS FLAGS (per law 5):** The check-partition argument (hash/offset/binding/provenance each killing a distinct failure) is **Supported** by the contract in the signal. The claim that the mechanism *achieves* bit-identity is **Unproven** until Test condition (3) runs — it is asserted here only as a falsifiable target, not a result. Stopping here: mechanism is buildable, test is falsifiable, success criteria met.",
