      "text": "# SELF ARCHAEOLOGY S1 - 2026-10-16 Classification: RECEIPT (audit; piles are PROPOSALS - the operator disposes) Producer: zcode-seat-20261016, three parallel read-only sweeps (VS Code stores, Codex store, Desktop + sibling projects) plus direct git checks. Commission: \"look at ourselves earnestly to see what we can bring forward, what was lost along the way, intelligently and compostably\" - back to the beginning, including grokbot's August databanks, old VS Code sessions, Codex, hand-backed-up copies, and Desktop folders. ## THE MAP (where the estate's memory actually lives) - Main git line: 1,088 commits, 2026-08-04 (\"Mag sovereign agent - clean publish baseline\") to now. git` (18 GB) is a full mirror - all The tracked line is intact BUT IT STARTS AT A PUBLISH BASELINE: whatever came before Aug 4 exists only in the untracked stores below. - VS Code seat: the AUGUST seat. All 367 keyword-matching History entries are August (zero in Sep/Oct). 68 Copilot agent sessions (Aug 7-29, largest 75 MB) in `AppData/Roaming/Code/User/workspaceStorage/e2b798e7. plus 289 MB of pre-edit file snapshots (5,823 versions) that hold code DELETED from the repo. - Codex seat: Aug 4 - Sep 24, 224 session rollouts (682 MB). folded into `corpus/oral_history/seat_pools/` (3,590 session files there across codex+grok) - THE FOLD PATHWAY EXISTS. 31 Sept sessions unfolded. 29 attachment dirs of pasted work product, Aug 6 - Sep 16. 3 GB, `state. 9 GB (mtime Sep 15) - the big untapped One Cursor transcript detected-but-never-imported (lead in - Grok Bot desktop: 76 MB local app data (`AppData/Roaming/Grok Bot`). August databanks the operator named are the app's conversation memory - reachable only by DRIVING the owned seat (lane law: seat-drive first). - The hand-backup: `Desktop/New folder/` (241 MB, Aug 2 - Oct 6) is the real one, holding the PRE-BASELINE era: `LIFT_ALL_SHIPS_FRAMEWORK. md` (Mar 28! IRO perspective-cartography log (Jun 25), cold-reader seeds (Jul 18), embassy close records (Aug 21-22), wake-up kit (Aug 9), frontier-crosscheck RIBs (Aug 10-11), ractor salon raw logs (Sep 9-10, 575 KB), session exports. `Desktop/Mag/` is an empty shell. - Siblings: `mycelial-republic` (constitution repo, live), `mag-sovereign-kit` (Jul 31/Aug 2 - pre-baseline), `sovereign-mirror` (Jul 10), `field-strike- the-chord` (Jun 9 - the earliest estate-adjacent date found), `mag-current-rebuild` (superseded), `lsa_reboot_staging` (duplicate docs), `Documents/Codex/` dated workspaces (Aug 4 - Sep 17). - Falsifier index: NOT lost - lives inside the main repo at `falsifier-index/`, updated 10/15. (Register row C10 corrected; a redundant clone made and removed this day. ## PILE ONE - BRING FORWARD (candidates, with routes) The Aug 6 Verkle design day (8 Codex attachments: \"MAG CONSTITUTION + REPOSITORY AUDIT\", \"Project Verkle: DeepSeek Fourth-Model Synthesis\", \"Synthesis for DeepSeek\", \"Grok Build Handoff\", convergence essay, build plan) - the founding multi-model salon chain, no clean copies in the repo. Route: fold to `corpus/oral_history/foundations/`. Aug 30 Codex outputs (13 artifacts: LESSIG salon synthesis, self-audit socratic salon, shadow-work salon, basecamp organ audit, model library bootstrap + atlas, board packs) - none in the repo; salon corpus holds only 0908/0914. Route: `corpus/salon/20260830/`. The deleted mag/ modules recoverable from VS Code snapshots (Aug 10-16): deleted - possibly deliberately. Route: stage under a `recovered/` holding dir for operator triage; compost-or-restore per file. Pre-baseline founding docs from the hand-backup (LIFT_ALL_SHIPS Mar 28, IRO cartography Jun 25, cold-reader Jul 18, EMBASSY-REPLY-CLOSE Aug 21, wake-up kit, frontier-crosscheck RIBs, OPERATOR_DRIVE Aug 29, the Ising machines research brief Aug 29). Route: `corpus/oral_history/prebaseline/`. The 31 unfolded Codex Sept sessions + the 68 VS Code chat sessions. Route: the existing oral_history seat_pools fold, one command family. Ractor salon raw logs (Sep 9-10) + session exports (hello-20260915. Route: `projects/ractor-salon` / corpus. The Matthew bundle (Sep 17 Codex workspace: puzzle art, canon audio, projection work, 714 KB audit evidence). Route: the Matthew corpus shelf. S2 digs: Cursor 1. 9 GB db; the never-imported Cursor transcript; Grok Bot August databanks via a desktop drive of the owned app; the Aug 26 session that ended with UNAPPLIED edits (61 MB - what was it writing? ## PILE TWO - LOST (acknowledged, not recoverable or partially) gz` - receipted \"shipped\" Aug 30, tarball gone everywhere; content partially reconstructible from the 37 KB transcript. - Desktop/Mag + Desktop/MagOutput originals (deleted; wake-up kit survives in the hand-backup copy + two History copies). - 9 lost notebooks (. ipynb) - snapshots hold metadata only; cell contents gone. - Pre-Aug-4 git history (never in this line; the baseline is the root). - `Temp/embassy-t1-clone` (gone; its outbox LATEST. md survives as a snapshot). ## PILE THREE - COMPOST (propose; demotion register rows after operator nod) - `Desktop/Mag/` empty shell; `Desktop/New folder (2)/` (browser extension, not estate); Binural / Kung Fu / Siggy / music-ai (personal media - marked NOT-ESTATE so future sweeps skip them; never touched). - `mag-current-rebuild/` (superseded; verify zero unique content first), `lsa_reboot_staging/` (duplicates), Desktop duplicate receipts already in watch/inbox (MODEL_RIB_LIBRARY_DESIGN_2026-08-31, PACK_SECRET_GATE_20260926), the loose projects-root strays (ui_*. xml, phonesalon pngs, farm receipts - fold to a receipts folder or leave), `Documents/_table_fix_scratch/` (falsifier tooling outside the tree - recover the tests, compost the rest). - Compost ledger: `memory/fold_history/SUPERSEDED. md` is the destination for whatever the operator rules dead; every compost row names what died and why. ## THE ONE-PARAGRAPH MORAL August was the VS Code/Codex era and it is almost entirely recoverable - the founding documents, the salons, the deleted modules, the raw sessions. tracked line begins at an Aug 4 publish baseline, so the true beginning (March-July) survives only in the hand-backup and the sibling repos. machinery already exists (oral_history seat_pools); what was missing was the Nothing here should be bulk-copied: each pile item gets a routing decision, and what dies gets a compost row instead of a silent deletion. ## WIRED THIS SITTING (per \"just wire it all in\") queued to the free-lane 24/7 dispatcher (preregistered studies A and B's design legs; receipts will land in watch/inbox/hermes_burn/). - Study C's 30-day observation cadence registered as a standing TODO in `watch/inbox/outerweb_research_20261013/WIRING_20261016. - Falsifier index register row corrected (alive, in-repo, updated 10/15).",
