    "14caf8a25d452044": {
      "text": "# SELF STEAL - the horizon object mapped to the estate (2026-10-16) Classification: CARD (self-steal pass on the horizon. v1 design; companion to watch/inbox/HORIZON_OBJECT_20261016. Producer: zcode-seat-20261016 Method: the SELF_STEAL discipline - every gap the design needs, mapped to an | horizon need | estate mechanism (age) | state | | append-only hash-chained object | verkle knots + `memory/proofs/anchored. jsonl` + `watch/inbox/index_events. jsonl` (14,732 events) + drift-patrol sha pins | live for months | | the bulk anchor (volume committed to one root) | `rib_boot. verkle_root` anchored at `memory/biography/verkle_tip. json`; core law: \"chain=record, window=reasoning; never store the window as truth\" | live | | surface pins (the ever-shifting surface) | `memory/mesh/delta_index. json` (sha256 + mtime per memory file) | live, the exact pattern | | trajectory scalars | census vector (5,158 / 611 / 0, minted today), zknot self-steal meter, `ROLLUP_DELTA. json` delta-math pattern | live | | the connective field (residual edges between sessions) | `mag. json` with n_bonds / n_moves / n_conflicts, `residual_json`, session brief, and a `verkle_hint` straight to the tip | live, one command | | the exit clause | `mag. )` - the signature literally takes a STATE HASH; `queue/handoff/*. json` brief-attached pattern (since Aug 3); `memory/warm_state. json` (chain, deployments, session_brief, verify) | live | | parseable-grammar law (machine-readable exits) | B2-249 carrier shape law (census claims must keep machine-parseable grammar or the gate fail-closes) | live, battle-tested by the 2-day fossil incident | | mint locking (one horizon per session exit) | instance_guard O_EXCL claim/release | live | | the wave field | mag/hydrology. py (integer head gradients), percolator half-life decay, pheromone field | live | | classification target | percolate() (SIGNAL/THEATER/NOISE) + drift-patrol | live | | the no-self law | DNA constitution, from the beginning: \"Fidelity lives in files + chain, not in a process that must stay awake\"; chariot: self=null, parts_only=true | live | ## The old mechanisms that are NEW AGAIN this sitting - The DNA formula - residual + registry + leaf = filed workday - turns out to be the horizon schema written in words. The horizon is its math encoding; DNA said it before the physics metaphor arrived. - `capture_summary` has carried a `state_hash` parameter in plain sight - the horizon's self_hash concept was sitting unused in a signature we call every - `bonds` was already emitting a per-session `verkle_hint` - the horizon's bulk anchor has been computed all along. We never chained the outputs. - The carrier shape law (B2-249), written to stop fabricated census counts, is the same law a horizon needs so no window can fabricate its own exit. json` (brief attached, not full chat) has been the horizon's transport doctrine since August; the horizon just makes the brief ## The gap - and it is one wire Nothing needs inventing. The single missing organ is a COMPOSER (~50 lines): call bonds (residual + counts + verkle hint), read the census vector, hash the touched surfaces, evaluate the exit predicates from beacon bytes, append Wiring, not inventing - the same verdict as the first self-steal: the estate did not copy the field, and it did not lose the mechanism; it never chained the last three commands together. ## Falsifier (carried from the design card, restated for the steal) If a horizon minted from these organs cannot let a cold window act without reopening the bulk, the composer under-selected its surface - fix the fields, not the stores. If horizon size ever correlates with session length instead of surface crossings, it has become a transcript with delusions.",
