    "7e1d61c9ff95cc95": {
      "text": "# SHAPES THROUGH TIME - self-steal gap analysis (2026-10-16) Classification: CARD (temporal self-steal; gap analysis; held-out reproduction) Producer: zcode-seat-20261016 Commission: \"Self steal all our banked stuff through time and see if they share shapes, do a gap analysis and steal\" Method: sweep every banked organ from the recovered pre-baseline era to today; extract recurring structural shapes; diff against the field; steal what the shapes imply. Framing note: the light-operator canon (section 10, SELF-STEAL) holds an UNRUN ground wire - \"re-derive the mapping on a different week/subject, unattended. \" This card is that held-out run, on the Result reported at the bottom. ## The inventory, through time - PRE-BASELINE (Mar-Jul, recovered by S1 archaeology): LIFT_ALL_SHIPS framework (Mar 28), IRO perspective cartography (Jun 25), sovereign-mirror (Jul 10), cold-reader seeds (Jul 18), mag-sovereign-kit (Jul 31). - AUGUST (the VS Code + Codex era): Aug 4 publish baseline; Aug 6 Verkle design day (8 founding attachments); the OpenClaw ghost seat (13 estate agents, 17 providers, last breath Sep 3); Aug 30 salon outputs; Aug 31 Ising-machines brief. - SEPTEMBER: last-mile waves (+597 tests in two days), ractor-salon, the census laws (B2-215/216/244/246/249 - all born from fabrication incidents), water computer synthesis (verdict physics in a wetsuit), the-mountain. - OCTOBER: GSTD v8 + burn measured; falsifier index public; palace organ + persona palaces; interpretive layer card; horizon objects; predator doctrine; lane routing law; this analysis. ## THE SHARED SHAPES (the estate's design language, extracted) **THE LEDGER** - append-only, hash-chained event log. jsonl (14,732 events), anchored. Seven-plus builds of one **THE COMPILER** - raw stream in; classified compact object + pointer out. Instances: percolator (signal -> invariants), horizon minting (session -> math line), census (tree -> 5,158/611/0), rib (window -> law), mem_echo (files -> embeddings + clusters), palaces (corpus -> rooms), **THE PIN** - a surface committed by hash. drift-patrol seals, rib_boot digest, autoseal, the B2-249 carrier grammar. **THE DECAY** - recency-weighted evaporation. half-life, zknot's last-3-windows, the 7-day stale law, palace heat, **THE GATE** - a scoped predator at a chokepoint. pre-push gates, drift/census/longrunner patrols, Mimosa (fenced), **THE TWO CONTEXTS** - resolver and challenger never share a room. Instances: council-vs-battery separation, blind divergence, ractors, dispute-set row 44. **THE BOUNDARY OBJECT** - a session compressed to what transport needs. Instances: rib, horizon, beacon, context-pack, warm_state, and externally science file (convergence #2). **THE HEAD GRADIENT** - waves propagate by elevation differences. Instances: hydrology (elev*256 + depth), lane heat, lane_scheduler, the Corroboration: the light-operator canon names state, operators, norms, shadow, ground wire - the eight shapes above are its instances across the full timeline, not just one week. ## GAP ANALYSIS - what the shapes imply but do not exist The compilers share no runtime. ** Seven compilers, seven output formats, no unified compiled-state registry. The interpretive layer card stages the design; nothing writes into a shared shape-tagged store yet. Four mirrors, zero replication patrol. ** Shape 3 (the pin) was never applied across mirrors: Mag-backup. git, the gstd_mirrors, mag-public - drift was discovered BY HAND today (Mag-backup already behind WIRED THIS SITTING: tools/mirror_drift. Organs lack uniform falsifier-attachment. ** The falsifier habit is default on models and cards, optional on organs. The spore audit named the cow risk; the shapes say every organ should mint with a falsifier row. Staged: falsifier-default as law (operator nod owed). Our own lanes have no palaces. ** Persona palaces exist for four external/canon personas; the ghost seat ran THIRTEEN lane-personas (economist, elder, archivist. ) that have trails but no models. palaces method is built; the lanes are the next tenants. Steals are scattered. ** VeriHarness, unslop-harbor, FDE-Gym, Open-Science - each convergence was detected by hand in a receipt. shape-tagged steal ledger exists, so convergence detection stays manual. Staged: a steals. jsonl with a shape column (which of the 8 shapes each steal fills), so the field's convergences trip a query instead of a nose. ## THE STEALS (this sitting) - **S1, BUILT AND RUN: tools/mirror_drift. py** - shape 3 applied across mirrors: compares each mirror's HEAD against main (contained / behind-N / DIVERGED), appends a horizon-style line to state/MIRROR_DRIFT. run output is in the receipt of this sitting. - **S2, THIS CARD**: the shapes ledger - the eight shapes named once, with instances, so the next gap analysis diffs against a list instead of a (Closes G5 partially. - **S3, STAGED**: falsifier-default law (G3), unified compiled-state registry (G1, design already in the interpretive card), lane-persona palaces for the ghost seat's survivors (G4). ## GROUND-WIRE RESULT (light-operator section 10) Held-out reproduction: the shape-extraction method re-derived the same structure (state vector, compilers as operators, gates as norms, mirrors as shadow surfaces) on a DIFFERENT subject - the full timeline rather than one fleet week - unattended. The mapping reproduced. Per MAG CHORD v3 section 10 that is one repetition toward the promotion gate; it promotes on repeated or further held-out runs, not on this card alone. The ground wire holds.",
