    "8314e9ae07b9489a": {
      "text": "# STEAL + ORPHAN REVISIT - antislop judge, nanobot, the OpenClaw ghost seat (2026-10-16) Classification: RECEIPT (design steal + orphan revisit) Producer: zcode-seat-20261016 Commission: \"Steal it and bring nanobot back in revisiting our orphans\" ## STEAL 1: unslop-harbor -> the riddler veil's consensus leg What was stolen (rawmodels/unslop-harbor, MIT/CC, ~4. - 200 RL tasks (100 tweet continuations from REAL human corpora + 100 HumanEval code bodies), EN/RU, each with TOML config, Dockerfile env, oracle solution, and a JSON RUBRIC (3-4 criteria). - The judge design: LLM grader scoring 0-10 PER RUBRIC CRITERION; a sigmoid preference term; a LENGTH-DEVIATION penalty beyond +/-15% of target word count; calibration tuned to 98. 3% human-preferred accuracy on held-out 011 per judge call. The wiring (design, staged for the veil organ): - The veil's consensus leg currently reads \"consensus = not run (mechanical The steal: promote the mechanical checks (8-gram copy-through, NO-DOX scan, stands declaration) to RUBRIC CRITERIA, and add the judge leg for what mechanics cannot grade - voice truth, stands honesty, the dark- entendre register - calibrated the unslop way: held-out pairs of VEIL-PASS'd estate prose vs known slop, human-preferred calibration (the estate corpus is the human-truth set; our VEIL-PASS archive is the Borrow their length-deviation penalty as the anti-bloat term. Eval data: unslop-harbor tasks. py are directly reusable for calibration smoke tests. First judge can be the free lane (sensing grade, findings only) before any paid calibration. - Trigger: next time the veil gate grades a parable where consensus matters (a contested or public-facing post). ## STEAL 2 / ORPHAN REVISIT: nanobot and the OpenClaw ghost seat Nanobot verdict (researched): REAL and maintained - HKUDS/nanobot, a ~4,000-line Python agent framework, the community's OpenClaw successor after OpenClaw's creator left for OpenAI (the repo sits at 160K+ stars, hence the Browser/terminal/chat surfaces, memory and web search Not installed here; no estate lane runs it yet. The orphan, inventoried this sitting - it is not a folder, it is a GHOST SEAT: openclaw/` still stands: agents/main/sessions with 138 session files (last active 2026-09-03), identity, logs/stability. - The pre-fix gateway snapshot (Documents/Codex/2026-08-30/wh/outputs/ pre-zai-fix. 2026-09-01. json - the only surviving pre-zai-fix state) shows a FULL ESTATE SEAT: 17 provider plugins enabled (zai x4 profiles, deepseek, groq, openrouter, xai, together, nvidia, ollama, google, anthropic, huggingface, mistral, cohere, cerebras, llama-cpp, openai); 13 configured agents named EXACTLY like the estate's lanes (main, worker, economist, ARCHIVIST, ractor, director, hands, tail, swarm, moonshot, gamedesigner, memory-worker, ELDER); estate skills mounted from /mag/. agents/skills (including a skill named ARCHIVIST - the bear had a namesake in OpenClaw before the operator drew him); a mag-file hook back into Mag; loop-detection circuit breakers; compaction safeguards; context pruning with cache-ttl; subagent delegation caps. - Model roster of the ghost: deepseek-v4-flash primary, glm-5. groq gpt-oss-120b, gpt-5. 6-sol, grok-4. 3, ollama qwen2. - Self-steal hit: the trails on the dashboard (economist. are these agents' trail files. The ghost seat was the estate's second body, and it died quietly on Sep 3. ## The port map (staged S4 - the wiring when the operator says deploy) | ghost seat organ | nanobot destination | | 17 provider plugins + model roster | nanobot model config (its provider surface is simpler; keep zai x4 + deepseek + ollama first) | agents/skills mount | nanobot skills/tools load (same dir, re-pointed) | | mag-file hook | needs a nanobot hook equivalent - THE critical leg (the seat talks to Mag through it) | | 13 agents (economist, elder, archivist. ) | nanobot multi-agent/subagent config - or a decision to resurrect only the 5 that earn their keep | | loop-detection + compaction safeguards | nanobot's guards + our horizon/percolator discipline as the substitute | | 138 orphan sessions | fold candidates to corpus/oral_history/seat_pools/openclaw_sessions (the codex fold pathway) | Contract note: the shared-surface contract's openclaw alias stays until a nanobot lane actually deploys; contract edits ride real lanes, not research. ## The line for the register The ghost seat died of the same disease the forgotten register hunts: it was wired, staffed with the estate's own agent names, and then nobody fed it. Nanobot is the cheaper body; the config is the soul; the port map is written.",
